.TH CVECTOR_APPEND_ARRAY 3 "2026-07-10" "c_collections" "C Collections Library - Functions"
.SH NAME
cvector_append_array \- append array of elements to vector
.SH LIBRARY
C Collections (libccollections, \-lccollections)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
#include <cvector.h>

bool cvector_append_array(cvec v, void *arr_ptr, size_t elem_count);
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
.nf
Appends an array of elements to the end of the vector. Automatically
reserves capacity if needed to hold all elements.
.fi
.SH PARAMETERS
.nf
v           Vector to append to
arr_ptr     Pointer to array of elements
elem_count  Number of elements in array
.fi
.SH RETURN VALUE
.nf
Returns true on success
Returns false if:
  - new total count would overflow or exceed max_elem_count
  - memory allocation fails
.fi
.SH NOTES
.nf
All elements are appended or none (atomic operation)
Automatically reserves capacity if needed
Elements are copied into the vector
Asserts if v is NULL
.fi
.SH "SEE ALSO"
.BR cvec_append_array (3),
.BR cvector_append_cvector (3)
